    "result_text": "Percentage discounts now round down to the cent, both on the whole invoice and on individual lines. The Playwright test passes in `bin/e2e`. The project has no unit tests (`src/test` doesn't exist), so that test is the only check that ran.\n\n**What changed** (all on the server, which works out every total; the front end only displays them):\n- **Line discounts:** `InvoiceLine.discount()` in `InvoiceLine.java` now rounds down instead of half up. For example, 15% of $100.05 is $15.00, not $15.01.\n- **Invoice discounts:** `Invoice.discount()` in `Invoice.java` now rounds a percentage discount down too. For example, 12.5% of $101.00 is $12.62, not $12.63.\n- **Comments:** I updated the descriptions of the rounding in `Invoice.java` and `invoice.service.ts` to match.\n\n**Rounding I left alone:** fixed-amount discounts, the discount cap, line totals (quantity \u00d7 price) and tax still round half up. The request only covered percentage discounts.",
